@startuml KTOB_09_sequence_recommendation
title KTOB - Consent-gated Recommendation Batch
actor Reader
participant "Angular" as UI
participant "Spring API" as API
participant "Reader / Privacy" as Privacy
participant "Advisor" as Advisor
database "Supabase PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "AI adapter" as AI
Reader -> UI : Request mode, prompt, exception IDs
UI -> API : POST /recommendations
API -> Privacy : verify JWT and ownership
Privacy -> DB : load current AI consent, personalization, boundaries
DB --> Privacy : effective policy
alt AI processing NOT authorized
 Privacy --> API : AI_PROCESSING_CONSENT_REQUIRED
 API --> UI : 403 problem+json; no provider call
else Processing authorized
 Privacy --> API : processing permitted
 API -> Advisor : create request / validate exceptions
 Advisor -> Privacy : validate explicit exception scope
 Privacy --> Advisor : request-scoped policy
 opt Personalization authorized AND usePersonalContext
  Advisor -> DB : read only permitted scoped history, notes, memories
  DB --> Advisor : filtered context (journal exclusions honored)
 end
 Advisor -> Privacy : recheck processing authorization before dispatch
 alt Consent revoked before dispatch
  Privacy --> Advisor : denied
  Advisor --> API : processing consent revoked
API --> UI : 403; no external request
 else Still authorized
  Privacy --> Advisor : allowed
  Advisor -> AI : prompt + explicitly authorized context
  alt AI provider unavailable
   AI --> Advisor : unavailable
   Advisor --> API : provider unavailable
API --> UI : 503 problem+json
  else AI response
   AI --> Advisor : candidate suggestions
   Advisor -> Privacy : verify boundaries and provenance
   Privacy --> Advisor : reject unsafe/unknown-as-safe candidates
   Advisor -> DB : save request and 0..N qualified items
   Advisor --> API : RecommendationResult(requestId, items[], providerStatus)
API --> UI : 200 RecommendationResult
  end
 end
end
note over Privacy,AI
Explicit AI-processing consent is mandatory for every call.
Personalization is a separate, default-off permission.
Revocation after dispatch cannot undo prior provider processing.
end note
@enduml
